              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A reversal loop runs `cur.next = prev` before `nxt = cur.next`. What is returned for 1→2→3?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`nxt` reads the already-overwritten `next`, so it is None",
                "The loop stops after one node",
                "Returns node 1 alone; 2 and 3 are lost"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "With `while fast and fast.next`, where does slow stop on 1→2→3→4?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Node 3, the second middle",
                "fast goes 1, 3, None while slow goes 1, 2, 3"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Next greater element on [2,1,3] with a decreasing index stack: what is the answer array?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "[3, 3, -1]",
                "3 pops index 1, then index 0",
                "Index 2 never pops, so it stays -1"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Why is `q.pop(0)` a poor dequeue, and what replaces it?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It shifts every remaining element, so O(n)",
                "Use `deque.popleft()`, which is O(1)"
